From: PS4 port
Subject: [PATCH] orbis: the libretro-common files this link can use, and the ones it cannot

melonDS DS fetches libretro-common with FetchContent and names the files it wants one by one.
Three of those names are wrong for a static PS4 module, in both directions.

⚠ THE CORE'S OWN LINK IS A SHARED MODULE EVERYWHERE ELSE, AND THAT HIDES TWO OF THESE.
melondsds_libretro is a MODULE library on every other platform, and a shared object may leave a
symbol undefined for the dynamic loader to find later. This port links every object into one
static .prx with no loader, so:

    ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: strcasestr_retro__
    >>> referenced by file_list.c

  + compat/compat_strcasestr.c. lists/file_list.c calls strcasestr, compat/strcasestr.h rewrites
    that to strcasestr_retro__ wherever the platform has none of its own, and the file that
    defines it was not in the list. It is sitting right there in the fetched tree.

    ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: rxml_load_document
    >>> referenced by logiqx_dat.c

  - formats/logiqx_dat/logiqx_dat.c. Its only undefined symbol is rxml_load_document, and the
    obvious fix - add formats/xml/rxml.c beside it - does not work here:

        rxml.c:30:10: fatal error: '../../deps/yxml/yxml.h' file not found

    rxml parses with yxml, which lives in RetroArch's deps/ and NOT in the libretro-common
    repository this core fetches, so that file cannot be built from this tree at all. Nothing in
    the core references logiqx_dat_* - checked over every object in the build - and a DAT-file
    reader is not something melonDS DS uses. Dropping the caller is the honest fix; adding a
    parser the fetched tree does not contain is not.

⚠ AND ONE FILE THAT THIS TREE ALREADY HAS A BETTER COPY OF.

  - dynamic/dylib.c. Its ORBIS arm does not compile against this SDK - it calls dlerror() with
    nothing declaring it and casts to a SceKernelModule these headers do not name - and the copy
    in RetroArch's own libretro-common, which this port has fixed, is linked into every core
    anyway as liborbis-retro-common.a. dylib_load, dylib_proc, dylib_close and dylib_error are
    all defined there, so removing the fetched one costs nothing and stops the error.

    ⚠ Turning HAVE_DYNAMIC off instead is not the way out: it also turns off
    HAVE_NETWORKING_DIRECT_MODE, which is what puts melonDS's pcap header on the include path,
    and the core's own net/net.cpp and platform/lan.cpp name melonDS::AdapterData and PCAP_IF_*
    whether that mode is configured or not.

diff --git a/cmake/libretro-common.cmake b/cmake/libretro-common.cmake
index cb2c495..131deab 100644
--- a/cmake/libretro-common.cmake
+++ b/cmake/libretro-common.cmake
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ target_sources(libretro-common PRIVATE
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/audio/resampler/drivers/sinc_resampler.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/compat/compat_fnmatch.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/compat/compat_posix_string.c
+    ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/compat/compat_strcasestr.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/compat/compat_strldup.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/compat/fopen_utf8.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/encodings/encoding_base64.c
@@ -26,7 +27,6 @@ target_sources(libretro-common PRIVATE
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/formats/image_texture.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/formats/image_transfer.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/formats/json/rjson.c
-    ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/formats/logiqx_dat/logiqx_dat.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/formats/m3u/m3u_file.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/formats/png/rpng.c
     ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/formats/png/rpng_encode.c
@@ -66,12 +66,6 @@ add_common_definitions(libretro-common)
 target_include_directories(libretro-common PRIVATE ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/src/libretro)
 target_compile_definitions(libretro-common PRIVATE HAVE_GLSYM_PRIVATE HAVE_RPNG)
 
-if (HAVE_DYNAMIC)
-    target_sources(libretro-common PRIVATE
-        ${libretro-common_SOURCE_DIR}/dynamic/dylib.c
-    )
-endif ()
-
 if (HAVE_EGL)
     target_link_libraries(libretro-common PUBLIC OpenGL::EGL)
 endif ()
